WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.961
Here's how to add 404 Missing to your website.

00:00:03.402 --> 00:00:08.162
Start with Node twenty-two or later, then install the release linked in the README.

00:00:08.603 --> 00:00:15.000
For United States appeals, request your own NCMEC access using the API access guide.

00:00:15.667 --> 00:00:19.011
Next, add the missing children API route to your server.

00:00:19.336 --> 00:00:21.437
Copy the configuration from the README.

00:00:21.762 --> 00:00:27.300
Keep your provider credentials in server-only environment variables, and use a private token store.

00:00:27.741 --> 00:00:30.760
Never put those keys in your page or browser bundle.

00:00:31.433 --> 00:00:33.476
Now open the guide for your framework.

00:00:33.918 --> 00:00:35.717
React and Vue have adapters.

00:00:36.158 --> 00:00:40.013
Astro, Ember, and plain HTML use the web component.

00:00:40.396 --> 00:00:46.038
Add it to your existing 404 page, point it at your API route, and choose a country.

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:48.244
Keep your home link visible.

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:51.605
Finally, visit a URL that doesn't exist.

00:00:51.988 --> 00:00:57.967
Check that it still returns HTTP 404 and that the official appeal or directory link works.

00:00:58.409 --> 00:01:03.436
The UK currently uses an official directory link while partner feed access is arranged.

00:01:03.819 --> 00:01:07.476
Copy the exact steps from the README, and you're ready to start.
